2026-05-10 11:46:10,686 - INFO - 
2026-05-10 11:46:10,686 - INFO - ### Why you might be wrong (or partially right):
2026-05-10 11:46:10,686 - INFO - - Your claim that private healthcare has lower costs isn't entirely accurate in most developed contexts. While private providers can sometimes offer faster access or specialized services at competitive prices (e.g., in some elective procedures or in countries with mixed systems), they often end up being more expensive overall due to higher premiums, out-of-pocket expenses, and profit-driven pricing. For example, in the U.S., private health insurance premiums have risen faster than inflation, burdening individuals and employers.
