2026-05-10 12:49:49,623 - INFO - - Psychological and evolutionary perspectives, such as those from scholars like Pascal Boyer or Daniel Dennett, argue that religious beliefs may arise from innate human cognitive traits, like our tendency to attribute agency to natural events or seek purpose in life. This makes it highly likely that religions are human constructs, even if they incorporate elements that feel divine to believers.
